note The io-clipboard crate: the one place the program reads or writes the system clipboard, through arboard with no image support. open, read and write each return a ClipboardError naming which failed. Only platform calls it, and only in a run with a real window: a script or screenshot run keeps a clipboard of its own, so scenarios never touch the user's clipboard and play the same everywhere.

